# rfc-002-video-management.mdc

## Title
RFC 002 – Video Management (YouTube-Based)

## Summary
This RFC outlines the structure and implementation of the video management system for the platform. It focuses on YouTube video embedding, metadata storage, category/tagging, and basic CRUD operations.

---

## Goals
- Add videos via YouTube URL
- Automatically fetch metadata: title, duration, thumbnail
- Enable categorization and tagging of videos
- Display videos in a responsive card layout with preview support

## Database Tables
### `videos`
| Field         | Type      | Description                       |
|---------------|-----------|-----------------------------------|
| id            | uuid      | Primary key                       |
| title         | text      | Video title                       |
| description   | text      | Optional description              |
| youtube_url   | text      | Full YouTube URL                  |
| youtube_id    | text      | Extracted YouTube video ID        |
| duration      | interval  | Video length                      |
| thumbnail     | text      | YouTube thumbnail URL             |
| category_id   | uuid      | Foreign key to `categories`       |
| tags          | text[]    | Array of tags                     |
| created_by    | uuid      | User ID who added the video       |
| created_at    | timestamp | Timestamp                         |

### `categories`
| Field       | Type    | Description            |
|-------------|---------|------------------------|
| id          | uuid    | Primary key            |
| name        | text    | Category name          |
| description | text    | Optional detail        |
| order       | int     | Carousel sort order    |

## API Integration
- Use YouTube Data API v3 to fetch:
  - title
  - duration
  - thumbnail

## Frontend Implementation
- Add video modal (Team Lead / Admin only)
- YouTube preview iframe embed
- Display grid of video cards (responsive, with filters)
- Category carousel component on homepage

## Role Permissions
- Admin: Full video CRUD
- Team Lead: Create/update videos
- User: View assigned/public videos
- Guest: View limited preview

## Validation
- Only valid YouTube URLs allowed
- Prevent duplicate YouTube IDs
- All required metadata must be available

## Timeline
**Sprint 2**
- Setup `videos` and `categories` tables
- Integrate YouTube API
- Implement video creation and list UI

